Summary
It’s better to separate application code and database storage.

Caching is essential for speed—can be done at browser, CDN, local server, or in-memory cache.

Handle cache invalidation and eviction carefully to avoid staleness and overflowing cache.

Use strategies like TTL, write-through/write-back/write-around, and proper eviction methods.
